WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:04.471
NARRATOR: Historically,
shark attacks on Reunion

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.573
have been rare.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:10.143
Over the previous decade,
the annual average

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.413
was just one incident.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.550
But in 2011, the
island is in crisis.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:26.459
Mathieu is actually Reunion's
fifth victim this year.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:29.229
And it's only September.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:32.132
Islanders are in shock.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.868
It's vitally important
that we find out

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.804
the reasons for these attacks.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:40.507
There is a real problem here.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.509
LORIS GASBARRE: We noticed
that something was changing.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.309
What?

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.677
We didn't know.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:47.881
NARRATOR: Residents are
desperate for answers.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:52.185
Their safety and their
livelihood is at stake.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.387
LORIS GASBARRE: A small
island lives with tourism.

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:56.423
If we don't have
tourism tomorrow,

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.426
we'll have nothing left.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:03.596
NARRATOR: So what's triggering
this deadly spate of attacks?

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.933
To find out, the French
government calls in leading

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.803
shark expert Geremy Cliff.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:12.439
Clearly alarm
bells were signaling.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:15.175
Five shark attacks of
which two were fatal.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.243
That is a huge spike.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.579
NARRATOR: Cliff believes
the first step to solving

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:23.016
this mystery and
preventing further attacks

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:27.086
is to identify the
species responsible.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:30.590
So he starts by analyzing
Mathieu's incident.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:33.793
And a chilling
details stands out.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.496
He was attacked by two sharks.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:46.473
MALE: [speaking french]

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:53.146
NARRATOR: A double shark attack
like this is extremely rare.

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:56.449
In fact, it's thought that
such an event has only

00:01:56.516 --> 00:02:00.353
been captured on film once.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.289
In the year 2000
in South Africa,

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:06.526
a teenager is surfing, when
he's suddenly knocked off

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:13.466
his board by one shark
while a second shark

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:16.936
attempts to bite him.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:19.706
Incredibly, the boy survives.

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:26.579
But this tag-team tactic
may serve as a calling card

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:29.015
for the culprit in Reunion.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:33.586
GEREMY CLIFF: Only certain
shark species hunt together.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:36.856
NARRATOR: Hammerheads search
for food in large schools

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:40.860
that can consist of
more than 100 sharks.

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:44.297
And lemons conduct
coordinated assaults

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:48.067
by herding prey into one area.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:52.071
Even blacktips hunt in
groups in the shallows.

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:55.441
But Cliff thinks
these species are all

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:58.411
too small to inflict
the kind of damage

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:00.613
that caused Mathieu's death.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.948
GEREMY CLIFF: One of
the striking features

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:07.554
of this particular attack is
the severe injuries involved.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:12.125
NARRATOR: Such ferocity points
to a much larger predator.

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:16.195
And only two species
commonly found in the region

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.830
fit that bill.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:22.669
GEREMY CLIFF: Firstly,
we have the tiger shark.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:26.439
Tiger sharks reach
at least 16 feet.

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:30.310
They have the size, in
terms of jaws and body size

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.745
to be able to tackle large prey.

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:37.483
And therefore, they won't be
scared of attacking a human.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.887
NARRATOR: Yet, Cliff
doubts tigers are to blame.

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.755
They are totally
solitary animals

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:45.291
and will hunt on their own.

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:50.063
NARRATOR: That leaves
only one possible culprit.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:54.133
To explain, Cliff turns to
footage recently captured off

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:57.770
the coast of Reunion, as part
of a study on the behavior

00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:00.239
of the region's sharks.

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:03.843
It depicts one particular
species that apparently

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:07.380
plays well with others.

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:10.183
GEREMY CLIFF: It shows clear
evidence of two sharks swimming

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:13.853
together, one behind the other.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:18.057
In fact, in nearly 20% of
occasions captured on film,

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:20.593
they were seen
foraging together.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:25.598
The sharks seen here
are bull sharks.

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:29.002
NARRATOR: Bull sharks
weigh as much as 500 pounds

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:31.537
and are highly aggressive.

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:36.943
They typically attack on their
own, often head-butting prey

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.646
before tearing it to shreds.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:42.815
But as these images
reveal, they also

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:45.284
use another hunting tactic.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.686
GEREMY CLIFF: There's
clearly an advantage

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:50.123
to work cooperatively
and thereby

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:53.993
prove predation efficiency.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.662
NARRATOR: Based
on this evidence,

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:58.031
Cliff believes he's
identified the type

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:00.099
of shark that killed Mathieu.

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:01.167
GEREMY CLIFF: So
from that I would

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:03.503
conclude that a bull
shark was responsible

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.471
for this particular attack.

